  {
   "id": 5,
   "kind": "notes",
   "report": true,
   "open": true,
   "name": "Protocol",
   "html": "<h2>Michaelis\u2013Menten (Km and Vmax)</h2><p>Each well gets a different substrate concentration. The plate is read kinetically and each well's Vmax becomes one point of the substrate curve; the graph fits v = Vmax\u00b7[S]/(Km + [S]).</p><p><b>Layout.</b> A 2-fold substrate series from 0.0625 to 8 mM across columns 1\u20138, in triplicate (rows A\u2013C). No-substrate wells A9\u2013C9 are the plate blank. Change the series in the template (Series button) so that it spans roughly 0.2 \u00d7 Km to 5 \u00d7 Km.</p><p><b>Results.</b> Km and Vmax with standard errors are in the Substrate table summaries; the graph legend also shows the confidence intervals, and the shaded band is the 95 % confidence band. Fit Options can weight the points or fix a parameter.</p><p>Vmax here is in mOD/min, as measured. To convert to concentration per minute divide by (\u03b5 \u00d7 path length).</p>",
   "summaries": [],
   "show_formulas": false
  },
